    "id": "prop:gamma-one-regression",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Regression corollary: when \\(\\Gamma=1\\), \\(D_P=\\{\\Delta_P\\}\\), \\(C_P(\\Delta_P)=0\\), and \\(\\mathcal I_P(\\rho)=\\{\\Delta_P\\}\\) for every \\(\\rho\\geq0\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\Gamma",
      "D_P",
      "\\Delta_P",
      "C_P",
      "\\mathcal I_P(\\rho)",
      "\\rho"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:sharp-frontier"
    ],
    "justification": "This regression corollary checks that the frontier collapses to the standard identified ATE when hidden assignment distortion is excluded.",
    "gap": "This is a required sanity reduction rather than a novelty claim.",
    "consumer": "Software and applied analyses obtain the usual observed-law ATE exactly at the no-confounding benchmark.",
    "proof_tex": "When \\(\\Gamma=1\\), \\(\\ell_x=u_x=e_x\\). Every positive response-type cell under a compatible law therefore has \\(q_{xij}=e_x\\), so \\(Z\\) is conditionally independent of \\((Y(0),Y(1))\\) given \\(X=x\\). Observational compatibility and consistency imply\n\\[\nE_Q[Y(1)\\mid X=x]=\\sum_jj\\pi_{1x,j},\\qquad\nE_Q[Y(0)\\mid X=x]=\\sum_ii\\pi_{0x,i}. \\tag{69}\n\\]\nSumming with weights \\(p_x\\) gives \\(T(Q)=\\Delta_P\\) for every \\(Q\\in\\mathcal H_1(P)\\). Also\n\\[\nd_{xij}=s_{xij}(q_{xij}-e_x)=0,\n\\]\nso \\(R_P(Q)=0\\).\n\nThe class is nonempty. In each stratum, couple \\(Y(0)\\) and \\(Y(1)\\) with marginals \\(\\pi_{0x,\\cdot}\\) and \\(\\pi_{1x,\\cdot}\\), for example by a product coupling, and draw \\(Z\\sim\\operatorname{Bernoulli}(e_x)\\) independently. The margin equations and consistency verify compatibility. Consequently\n\\[\nD_P=\\{\\Delta_P\\},\\qquad C_P(\\Delta_P)=0,\\qquad\n\\mathcal I_P(\\rho)=\\{\\Delta_P\\}\\quad\\text{for every }\\rho\\geq0.\n\\]",
